{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms","id":1024672,"title":"Japan supernaturals terms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-31T01:55:41-08:00","id":1024672,"title":"Japan supernaturals terms","content":"With <b>Hurt Locker</b> and it\u2019s written Tokyo setting, I\u2019m more and more eager to run game or even just stories in Japan crossover setting. As I have hard time to believe that local, for example, Uratha or Awakened populations would not translate European terms on their own language, I\u2019m here asking good folks knowing Japan or Japanese\u2019s to translate some core terms from the game lines on local variant in language of Nippon.<br /> <br /> Here is bunch of terms to start translation from English to Japanese \u2013 of course, I look here more on r\u014dmaji writing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Vampire</b><br /> General terms:<ul><li>Clan</li> <li>Vitea</li> <li>Humanity</li> <li>Blood Potency</li> <li>Prince</li> </ul><b>Werewolf</b><br /> Common tribes names:<ul><li>Blood Talons</li> <li>Bone Shadows</li> <li>Hunters in Darkness</li> <li>Iron Masters</li> <li>Storm Lords</li> <li>Fire-Touched</li> <li>Ivory Claws</li> <li>Predator Kings</li> </ul>General terms:<ul><li>Protectorate</li> <li>Sacred Hunt</li> <li>Host</li> <li>Spirit</li> <li>First Change</li> <li>Harmony</li> <li>Essence</li> <li>Primal Urge</li> </ul><b>Mage</b><br /> Paths \u2013 I think that Japan ( and Asian in general ) Awakened would follow possible Vinca culture ( see <i>Sundered World</i> <b>Dark Era</b> ) names for Paths \u2013 or based them on Five Elements ( see <b>Tome of Watchtower</b> more on this ). So we would have this list:<ul><li>Acanthus \u2013 Sky - Air</li> <li>Mastigos \u2013 Forest - Void ( Spirit )</li> <li>Moros \u2013 Water - Earth</li> <li>Obrimos \u2013 Storm \u2013 Fire</li> <li>Thyrsus \u2013 Blood \u2013 Water</li> </ul>Orders \u2013 In <i>To the Strongest </i><b>Dark Era</b> we have Indian names for Darshanas that will become Orders. Those names could be translated in to Japanese, but I think, in the end, Western terms would simply flourish in local translation after centuries of Awakened exchange. So let\u2019s stick to them.<ul><li>Adamantine Arrow \u2013 He is one difference I would make \u2013 Using <i>To the Strongest</i> Asian name of previous Darshana \u2013 \u2018Thunderbolt Weapon\u2019</li> <li>Free Council \u2013 Here it can even be just Japan for Council of Free Assemblies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li>Guardians of the Veil</li> <li>Mysterium \u2013 As Order from 12<sup>th</sup> century, simple translation on Japanese would be enough. If there is not good translation, maybe using meaning of original Indian darshana Jnanashakti - \u2018Power of Wisdom\u2019</li> <li>Silver Ladder</li> <li>Seers of the Throne</li> <li>Hegemony</li> <li>Panopticon</li> <li>Paternoster</li> <li>Praetorian</li> </ul>General terms:<ul><li>Path</li> <li>Order</li> <li>Consilium \u2013 Probably translation of Council will be enough</li> <li>Legacy</li> <li>Gnosis</li> <li>Mana</li> <li>Wisdom</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-31-2016, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T02:18:54-08:00","id":1024678,"title":"","content":"Aren't the Orders already translated in the 2e core?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T03:25:16-08:00","id":1024696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms?p=1024678#post1024678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't the Orders already translated in the 2e core?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, now I see I missed them. Still, Paths and other terms are not translated as I see in Tokyo setting.<br /> <br /> For ease of refereance, Japan's Orders names:<ul><li>The Adamantine Arrow - <i>Kongou no Ya</i></li> <li>The Free Council - <i>Jiyuu Hyougikai</i></li> <li>The Guardians of the Veil - <i>Shikiri no Shugosha</i></li> <li>The Mysterium - <i>Hiouden</i></li> <li>The Silver Ladder - <i>Gin no Hashigo </i></li> <li>The Seers of the Throne - <i>Zasho no Senkaku-sha</i></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T16:21:37-08:00","id":1024938,"title":"","content":"For me, I've refer to &quot;The Vigil&quot; as <b>Sadame</b> - it's a term that loosely means Destiny/Fate, but it also means Conviction, Choice, Determination. Of course, that's the translation I've found, but I could be wrong, and there's probably a term already made for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T17:30:12-08:00","id":1024952,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone's going to fight me especially hard on the common prosaic term for Beasts in Japan being <i>kaiju</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T17:45:56-08:00","id":1024956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms?p=1024952#post1024952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone's going to fight me especially hard on the common prosaic term for Beasts in Japan being <i>kaiju</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Obake</i> or <i>Bakemono</i> would also work, potentially to differentiate between different types of Beasts. <i>Kaiju</i> would work well for Anakim, given how Kaiju tend to be larger than life, literally. I do agree though, Kaiju works well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T02:14:25-08:00","id":1025035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms?p=1024956#post1024956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Obake</i> or <i>Bakemono</i> would also work, potentially to differentiate between different types of Beasts. <i>Kaiju</i> would work well for Anakim, given how Kaiju tend to be larger than life, literally. I do agree though, Kaiju works well.</div> </div> </div> </div>How they would translate Families then? With Anakim being <i>Kaiju</i>, Namtaru being <i>Bakemono </i>maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T10:54:27-08:00","id":1025115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms?p=1024956#post1024956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Obake</i> or <i>Bakemono</i> would also work, potentially to differentiate between different types of Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I picked <i>kaiju</i> because the kanji literally translate to &quot;strange beast.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Kaiju</i> would work well for Anakim, given how Kaiju tend to be larger than life, literally. </div> </div> </div>The conflation of <i>kaiju</i> with <i>daikaiju</i> is a relatively recent thing brought on by movies like Godzilla and Pacific Rim \u2014 the <i>kaijin</i> that serve as monsters-of-the-week in a lot of tokusatsu shows are a subset of <i>kaiju</i> whether they grow ten stories tall at the episode's climax or not.<br /> <br /> Family names would depend on what framework of nomenclature Japanese Begotten and/or their observers used to delineate the differences \u2014 the English names are an assortment of mythological creatures. The Namtaru are named for a Mesopotamian god of pestilence, the Makara are named for a Hindu threshold guardian whose particular variety of mercreature varies by region, the Anakim are named for a Biblical reference to a race of giants generally considered to draw descent from the offspring of fallen angels, the Ugallu are named for a bird-footed storm-demon who went on to be made a temple guardian, and the Eshmaki are named for the Georgian word for a devil, which itself derives from the name of a Zoroastrian demon of wrath opposed to the divinity of truth.<br /> <br /> That doesn't really translate readily to a uniform set of names for broad categories of monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T11:32:42-08:00","id":1025123,"title":"","content":"As someone who has had a strong interest in Kamen Rider for the past five years (to the point I'm trying to make a tokusatsu style Conspiracy for Hunter), that is genuinely interesting to know. Thank you for enlightening me on the subject <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T12:52:34-08:00","id":1025139,"title":"","content":"Hegemony: \u30d8\u30b8\u30a7\u30e2\u30cb\u30fc<br /> Mammon: \u30de\u30c3\u30e2\u30f3<br /> Panopticon: \u30d1\u30f3\u30aa\u30d7\u30c1\u30b3\u30f3<br /> Paternoster: \u30d1\u30c6\u30eb\u30ce\u30b9\u30bf\u30fc<br /> Praetorian: \u30d7\u30e9\u30a8\u30c8\u30ea\u30e3\u30f3<br /> <br /> Japanese Seers adopted Anglicized loanwords for their Ministries in a bungled attempt to promote neoliberal colonialism in the heyday of the eighties. After the economic bubble collapsed the project stopped mattering, but cultural inertia prevails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T16:23:35-08:00","id":1025193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms#post1024672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With <b>Hurt Locker</b> and it\u2019s written Tokyo setting, I\u2019m more and more eager to run game or even just stories in Japan crossover setting. As I have hard time to believe that local, for example, Uratha or Awakened populations would not translate European terms on their own language, I\u2019m here asking good folks knowing Japan or Japanese\u2019s to translate some core terms from the game lines on local variant in language of Nippon.<br /> <br /> Here is bunch of terms to start translation from English to Japanese \u2013 of course, I look here more on r\u014dmaji writing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Are you looking for more direct translations? When I've used Japanese in the various Tokyo sections, I tried to make them contextually relevant, and a lot of times I sort of inserted a secondary implied meaning. <br /> <br /> The closest thing to direct translation won't always mean common usage words, either. But then again, sometimes we don't favor common usage terminology in CofD. So it's a balancing act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T16:25:51-08:00","id":1025195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms?p=1025139#post1025139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hegemony: \u30d8\u30b8\u30a7\u30e2\u30cb\u30fc<br /> Mammon: \u30de\u30c3\u30e2\u30f3<br /> Panopticon: \u30d1\u30f3\u30aa\u30d7\u30c1\u30b3\u30f3<br /> Paternoster: \u30d1\u30c6\u30eb\u30ce\u30b9\u30bf\u30fc<br /> Praetorian: \u30d7\u30e9\u30a8\u30c8\u30ea\u30e3\u30f3<br /> <br /> Japanese Seers adopted Anglicized loanwords for their Ministries in a bungled attempt to promote neoliberal colonialism in the heyday of the eighties. After the economic bubble collapsed the project stopped mattering, but cultural inertia prevails.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are mostly okay. But I'd use \u30d1\u30f3\u30aa\u30d7\u30c6\u30a3\u30b3\u30f3 for Panopticon. Otherwise it sounds really weird and much further from the natural pronunciation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T16:31:03-08:00","id":1025196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms?p=1025195#post1025195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These are mostly okay. But I'd use \u30d1\u30f3\u30aa\u30d7\u30c6\u30a3\u30b3\u30f3 for Panopticon. Otherwise it sounds really weird and much further from the natural pronunciation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, fair. I think early on when learning Japanese I saw some word that used \u30c1 to stand in for &quot;ti&quot; and it just stuck with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T16:39:12-08:00","id":1025197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms?p=1025196#post1025196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, fair. I think early on when learning Japanese I saw some word that used \u30c1 to stand in for &quot;ti&quot; and it just stuck with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can? But it's not as common these days. They mostly did that because katakana wasn't so invested in direct emulation, and the \u30c1 sound was far more natural for native Japanese speakers. They've moved more toward \u30c6\u30a3though as English education's gotten significantly better, and pretty much everyone can seamlessly pronounce that sound instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T16:50:34-08:00","id":1025200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms?p=1025197#post1025197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can? But it's not as common these days. They mostly did that because katakana wasn't so invested in direct emulation, and the \u30c1 sound was far more natural for native Japanese speakers. They've moved more toward \u30c6\u30a3though as English education's gotten significantly better, and pretty much everyone can seamlessly pronounce that sound instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's really interesting. Thanks for the New Year's knowledge!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T18:10:20-08:00","id":1026791,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure on how you do pronounce &quot;Panopticon&quot; in the USA, but I always thought it would be more of a \u30ce than an \u30aa. So I would make it \u30d1\u30f3\u30ce\u30d7\u30c6\uff72\u30b3\u30f3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T18:12:49-08:00","id":1026792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms?p=1026791#post1026791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure on how you do pronounce &quot;Panopticon&quot; in the USA, but I always thought it would be more of a \u30ce than an \u30aa. So I would make it \u30d1\u30f3\u30ce\u30d7\u30c6\uff72\u30b3\u30f3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Typically, we'd pronounce it almost as if &quot;pan&quot; and &quot;opticon&quot; were two separate words. So I'd probably lean toward \u30aa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T23:29:35-08:00","id":1026882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms?p=1025139#post1025139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hegemony: \u30d8\u30b8\u30a7\u30e2\u30cb\u30fc<br /> Mammon: \u30de\u30c3\u30e2\u30f3<br /> Panopticon: \u30d1\u30f3\u30aa\u30d7\u30c1\u30b3\u30f3<br /> Paternoster: \u30d1\u30c6\u30eb\u30ce\u30b9\u30bf\u30fc<br /> Praetorian: \u30d7\u30e9\u30a8\u30c8\u30ea\u30e3\u30f3<br /> <br /> Japanese Seers adopted Anglicized loanwords for their Ministries in a bungled attempt to promote neoliberal colonialism in the heyday of the eighties. After the economic bubble collapsed the project stopped mattering, but cultural inertia prevails.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only that Ministries are from XVI century and show in almost all world instantly ( they reconnected all previous Seers cults under thumb of Ministers in few years time ). I do not very see Seers of Edo period taking Latinized names for their Ministries as half of them <i>would be on</i> Shoguns Court. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We talk here about circa 1500, plus few years at most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-05-2017, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T01:11:05-08:00","id":1026912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms?p=1026882#post1026882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only that Ministries are from XVI century and show in almost all world instantly ( they reconnected all previous Seers cults under thumb of Ministers in few years time ). I do not very see Seers of Edo period taking Latinized names for their Ministries as half of them <i>would be on</i> Shoguns Court. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We talk here about circa 1500, plus few years at most.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're misreading the proposal. The idea is that in the 1980s the Seers in Japan adopted the use of the English names for their ministries. They were already established in Japan prior to that, they just had different names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T01:20:21-08:00","id":1026916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms?p=1026912#post1026912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're misreading the proposal. The idea is that in the 1980s the Seers in Japan adopted the use of the English names for their ministries. They were already established in Japan prior to that, they just had different names.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but what about this original Japanese terms for Seers? If I want to run story in Edo period I still do not know how to call local Ministries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T06:23:56-08:00","id":1026991,"title":"","content":"First of all, let me ask this - which Ministries would be present in your Edo-period story? Given what I know of Japanese and their relationship to religion, the Paternoster doesn't quite make sense to me; I could see arguments against using the Panopticon or Mammon as well. Would other Ministries based on one of the other seven Exarchs make sense for this era? Remember, Ministries do rise and fall all the time.<br /> <br /> Anyways! Paternoster, Panopticon, Hedgemony, and Praetorean seem to be greek words relating to Father, Eye, Leader and General. In short, they're rough greek translations for the names of the Exarchs. If you want japanese-native terms for the Ministries, I would say just run the Exarch's english name through a translator. That seems to be roughly how we got the current ones being used. The Ministries are the Fallen World embodiments of the Supernal Exarch, they are one and the same, so it makes sense for mage hubris to adopt the Exarch's name as the organization's name.<br /> <br /> The shogunate was a major influence in japan, so I would put the General as the big Ministry in charge, and use Shogun as the name. I would be tempted to equate the emperor and other nobility of Japan with the Union, and just use Tennou as the Exarch/Ministry name. The four big religions that shaped japan during this period are Christianity, Confucianism, Buddhism and Shintoism; the first three are actually imported from other regions, so they would carry Chinese or Greek names. Shintoism is the only one that would use native japanese terms, and even then, its highly inappropriate for the Father. Each religion rose and fell in prominance during the Edo period; I would reflect this by saying there's a few seer organizations serving different proto-Ministries fighting it out to become a dominant Ministry of the region.<br /> <br /> The merchant and artist class was rising up during this period as well, reflecting a rise in the Chancelor's prominance, but were forbidden by law to have as much wealth (or, at least display as much) as the samurai class. While there are exceptions, I imagine this firmly puts the Chancellor as the underdog in Edo society. Jushou would be the translation here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-05-2017, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:17:23-08:00","id":1027072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024672-japan-supernaturals-terms?p=1026916#post1026916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, but what about this original Japanese terms for Seers? If I want to run story in Edo period I still do not know how to call local Ministries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see. I think I agree with MCN here. For Hegemony I think the best term would be <i>kenryoku</i> (\u6a29\u529b), which means political power or authority. The term &quot;panopticon&quot; doesn't enter common parlance until the 18th century with Jeremy Bentham's prison proposal, so that Ministry might not even exist in earlier times. The Japanese word for eye is <i>me</i> (\u76ee). Paternoster is tricky, since the Japanese conception of religion is a more fluid, though one could make arguments for Seer sects that try to impose <i>kegare</i> on as many things as possible, or make strict interpretations of Confucian law.<br /> <br /> Actually, it could be interesting if 1500s Japan were ruled by a Ministry that today is either vanishingly rare or that has died out completely. Something dedicated to the Ruin or the Nemesis, maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T13:07:53-08:00","id":1027239,"title":"","content":"The portuguese arrived in Japan at the middle of 16th century, and they left a mark in Japanese language, also introducing christianism. At least some Seers could have used Portuguese names until the 80s. Those could either be distinct spellings of the more common names, or actual translations to Portuguese.<br /> <br /> <i>Common//Spelling//Portuguese</i><br /> Hegemony//\u30a8\u30b8\u30a7\u30e2\u30cb\u30a2//\u30ea\u30c7\u30e9\u30f3\u30b5<br /> Mammon//\u30de\u30e2\u30f3//\u30ea\u30b1\u30b6<br /> Panopticon//\u30d1\u30ce\u30d7\u30c6\u30a3\u30b3//\u30bb\u30f3\u30c6\u30a3\u30cd\u30c3\u30e9<br /> Paternoster//\u30d1\u30c6\u30eb\u30ce\u30b7\u30c6\u30eb//\u30d1\u30c9\u30ec\u30ce\u30c3\u30bd<br /> Praetorian//\u30d7\u30ec\u30c8\u30ea\u30a2\u30aa\u30f3//\u30de\u30b8\u30b9\u30c8\u30e9\u30c9","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}